# DARSID COMMUNITY RULES

## 1. Respect each other

Treat people like actual human beings. No bullying, harassment, discrimination, or purposely trying to make someone's day miserable.

## 2. No unnecessary drama

Disagreements happen, but don't turn every little argument into a whole server-wide war. If there's a problem, handle it calmly or ask a moderator for help.

## 3. Keep things appropriate

Don't post NSFW, sexually explicit, or seriously disturbing content. Keep the server comfortable for the people who are here.

## 4. No spam

Don't flood chats with messages, emojis, pings, or random links. Give everybody else a chance to speak too!

## 5. Use the right channels

Try to keep messages in their proper channels. If there's a channel for a specific topic, that's probably where it belongs.

## 6. No unwanted advertising

Don't advertise your own server, social media, projects, or products without permission from the staff.

## 7. Protect your privacy

Don't share your own or someone else's private information without permission. This includes addresses, phone numbers, passwords, private messages, and other sensitive details.

## 8. No scams or suspicious links

Don't scam people, impersonate others, or send suspicious links and files. If something looks sketchy, don't click it. Tell a moderator immediately.

## 9. Listen to the staff

Moderators are here to help keep the place running. Follow reasonable staff instructions, and if you think a decision is unfair, discuss it respectfully instead of starting a fight.

## 10. No abusing pings

Don't repeatedly ping staff, creators, or other members for attention. Use pings when they're actually needed.

## 11. Keep your account yours

Don't share your password! Staff won't ask for your password. Even your friends shouldn't be trusted with your account credentials.

## 12. Don't exploit loopholes

Just because something isn't written word-for-word in these rules doesn't mean it's automatically okay. Use common sense, and don't deliberately ruin the experience for everyone else.

## What happens if you break the rules?

Depending on what happened, staff may give a warning, delete messages, timeout you, kick you, or ban you.

Thanks for being here, now go enjoy the place! :D

Want to know how to request a role, permission, etc.? Head to the Info channel to learn more.
